  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Macaroni cheese is cooked pasta stirred into a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "béchamel",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "bechamel"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " sauce loaded with cheddar, then baked in a dish with a crunchy breadcrumb topping. It comes out of the oven golden on top and bubbling underneath. The whole thing takes under an hour. The ratio of sauce to pasta matters: too little sauce and the baked version turns dry; this recipe has enough to keep it creamy even after baking."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
